## Root Cause
The use of 'mathjs.eval' on user-defined input can lead to arbitrary code execution, making the application vulnerable to injection attacks.

## Explanation
The patch replaces 'mathjs.eval' with 'mathjs.simplify' after validating the mathematical expression. This ensures that only safe mathematical operations are processed, thereby mitigating the risk of code injection.

